[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785915563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115279#issuecomment-3785915563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115279","id":3785915563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hqHyr","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T18:05:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T18:05:28Z","body":"cc @van800 @Ivorforce from the initial ticket","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785915563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786047109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115279#issuecomment-3786047109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115279","id":3786047109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hqn6F","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T18:33:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T18:33:47Z","body":"As mentioned in the previous issue, it would be possible to avoid this error print by using `p_params.get(\"checksum\", Array())`.\n\nHowever, it is questionable whether that is the correct fix. If the caller provides an invalid dictionary, should our DAP implementation print an error? Should it react and handle the error in some other way? \n\nI cannot comment on this decision as I'm not familiar with DAP. cc @godotengine/debugger ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786047109/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786086018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115279#issuecomment-3786086018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115279","id":3786086018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hqxaC","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T18:43:16Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T07:45:20Z","body":"The approach I took for LSP was to only use `get` were omitting the value is valid. Members that have to be present still use the standard `[\"\"]` and the error can be an indicator of either a spec change or an incompliant client.\n\nFor DAP it seems like omitting `checksums` is allowed. As well as `path` and `name`. (`name` is interesting though since the client is allowed to omit it, but the adapter is not, so this needs more insight than simply skimming the spec).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786086018/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786127324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115279#issuecomment-3786127324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115279","id":3786127324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hq7fc","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T18:53:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T18:53:10Z","body":"I'm testing a solution that validates as follows:\n\n- Elements that are required by the spec are asserted with `ERR_FAIL_COND(...)`, notifying both Godot and the DAP client what went wrong if triggered (no existing key/wrong type)\n- Elements that are optional by the spec follow the `dict.get(\"my_arg\", 0)` idiom, enforcing safe access with default values.\n\nWhat do you think?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786127324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786134737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115279#issuecomment-3786134737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115279","id":3786134737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hq9TR","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T18:54:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T18:54:55Z","body":"Sorry, forgot to add earlier; the error reported on checksums is indeed *fishy*. I'm also investigating the spec in more detail there to properly fix the reported issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786134737/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]